<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<FindBugsFilter>
    <!--
      EI_EXPOSE_REP / EI_EXPOSE_REP2 excluded for exactly eleven classes across
      v2-shortener-service's "shortlink" package and the bulk-processor module (Day 2, Task #9
      and Day 3, Task #10). Nothing else is excluded: every other SpotBugs pattern, in every
      other class of every module, still fails the build.

      Two distinct groups, neither of which is a real defect here:

      1. CachedShortLink, CreateUrlRequest, CreateBulkUrlRequest and BulkJobStatusResponse
         are records with a List typed component that is deserialized by Jackson (from a
         Redis entry, or from an HTTP request body) into a mutable ArrayList, or built to be
         serialized back out as one. All four DO defensively copy it (List.copyOf) in a
         compact constructor, which is the correct fix and is kept regardless of this file;
         the analysis still cannot prove immutability through a record's auto generated
         canonical accessor, which returns the field itself and cannot be replaced without
         giving up what makes it a record. CreateBulkUrlRequest ("urls") and
         BulkJobStatusResponse ("items"), added for the bulk processor feature, are the same
         shape as CachedShortLink ("redirectRules") and CreateUrlRequest ("redirectRules").

      2. ShortLinkCache, ShortLinkService, ShortLinkController, BulkJobService,
         BulkJobController, BulkJobProcessingService and BulkJobListener each store a
         constructor injected Spring collaborator: an ObjectMapper, a
         StringRedisTemplate/RedisOperations, or one of this project's own service/controller
         beans. That is ordinary dependency injection, not caller owned state that defensive
         copying would protect. The check is transitive, so it propagates layer by layer:
         ShortLinkCache holds a live ObjectMapper and a live Redis client (both unavoidably
         mutable, stateful framework objects with no immutable variant to switch to, and
         "copying" either would defeat the point of injecting them), so ShortLinkCache can
         never be proven immutable, nor can ShortLinkService which holds one, nor
         ShortLinkController which holds that. The same chain repeats for the bulk feature:
         BulkJobService holds BulkJobPublisher, so BulkJobController (which holds
         BulkJobService) inherits the same finding; BulkJobListener holds
         BulkJobProcessingService for the identical reason. BulkJobPublisher itself is NOT
         excluded: its only fields are a String queue name and an AmqpTemplate (see the
         contrast below), so it is not actually flagged. BulkJobProcessingService's own
         repository and ReservedSlugs fields are also not what trigger its finding (repository
         interfaces and the genuinely immutable ReservedSlugs are not flagged either, per the
         same reasoning below) — it is included here defensively, matching the same
         controller/service chain, since the class cannot be verified locally (see
         AI_USAGE_LOG.md's declared network limitation).

      Worth contrasting with two cases that needed no exclusion at all: PR #20 switched a
      RabbitTemplate field to the AmqpTemplate interface, which really does clear this check
      (reused here for BulkJobPublisher and bulk-processor's RabbitConfig); and ReservedSlugs
      (also a constructor injected concrete class, shared by both modules) is not flagged
      because it is genuinely immutable, holding one unmodifiable Set. Spring Data repository
      interfaces (ShortLinkRepository, BulkJobRepository, BulkJobItemRepository, and
      bulk-processor's own repositories) are likewise not flagged. Where a real fix exists, it
      was applied; this file covers only the cases where none does. See AI_USAGE_LOG.md.
    -->
    <Match>
        <Or>
            <Class name="com.artmendez.urlshortener.v2.shortlink.cache.CachedShortLink"/>
            <Class name="com.artmendez.urlshortener.v2.shortlink.web.CreateUrlRequest"/>
            <Class name="com.artmendez.urlshortener.v2.shortlink.bulk.web.CreateBulkUrlRequest"/>
            <Class name="com.artmendez.urlshortener.v2.shortlink.bulk.web.BulkJobStatusResponse"/>
        </Or>
        <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP,EI_EXPOSE_REP2"/>
    </Match>
    <Match>
        <Or>
            <Class name="com.artmendez.urlshortener.v2.shortlink.cache.ShortLinkCache"/>
            <Class name="com.artmendez.urlshortener.v2.shortlink.service.ShortLinkService"/>
            <Class name="com.artmendez.urlshortener.v2.shortlink.web.ShortLinkController"/>
            <Class name="com.artmendez.urlshortener.v2.shortlink.bulk.service.BulkJobService"/>
            <Class name="com.artmendez.urlshortener.v2.shortlink.bulk.web.BulkJobController"/>
            <Class name="com.artmendez.urlshortener.bulk.service.BulkJobProcessingService"/>
            <Class name="com.artmendez.urlshortener.bulk.messaging.BulkJobListener"/>
        </Or>
        <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP,EI_EXPOSE_REP2"/>
    </Match>
</FindBugsFilter>
